Host capture used the simulator Unix PTP socket:
  /tmp/.z80pack/intelmdssim.pt

For each guest command `COPY :F0:BYTRTN.<ext> TO :HP:`, capture the reported
directory LENGTH bytes after the zero leader and verify the zero trailer.
Observed file lengths were PLM 97, LST 1185, OBJ 165, SAT 173, LMP 399, LOC
130, MAP 400, and HEX 54 bytes. The per-transfer framing was 120 zero bytes,
payload, 120 zero bytes. Artifact files in this fixture contain only payload.

The HEX transfer was captured independently (294 framed bytes) and the other
seven transfers were captured over one persistent receiver connection. The
first byte of an exploratory repeated HEX stream had one fewer leading zero;
the separately captured 294-byte transfer was used for the preserved HEX
artifact. Payload lengths and hashes are checked in `manifest.json`.
